  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting and saying goodbye",
     "texto": [
      "**안녕하세요** can be used to greet anyone at any time of day.",
      "To say goodbye there are two phrases, depending on who is leaving. To someone who **is leaving**, you say **안녕히 가세요** («go in peace»). To someone who **is staying**, **안녕히 계세요** («stay in peace»).",
      "When meeting someone: **만나서 반갑습니다** (pleased to meet you), or the shorter **반갑습니다**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I am…",
     "texto": [
      "The verb «to be» is attached after the noun: **이에요** if the word ends in a consonant, and **예요** if it ends in a vowel.",
      "학생 → **학생이에요** (I am a student). 의사 → **의사예요** (I am a doctor).",
      "To ask a question nothing changes: you just raise your voice at the end. **학생이에요?** = Are you a student?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "«To be»: 이에요 / 예요",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "The word ends in",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "What you add",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "consonant",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "이에요",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "학생이에요 (is a student)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "vowel",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "예요",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "의사예요 (is a doctor)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "저는: «as for me»",
     "texto": [
      "**저** is «I», said politely. After it comes **는**, the **topic particle**, which shows what you are talking about: 저는 = «as for me».",
      "The particle is **는** after a vowel and **은** after a consonant: 저**는**, 이름**은**.",
      "**제** is «my»: **제 이름은 마리아예요** = my name is María.",
      "You add **씨** after the names of other people: 민수 씨. **Never** add it after your own name.",
      "In Korea the surname comes first: 김민수 is Minsu, with the surname Kim."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
